{"kind":"assert","text":"The in-flight seat-authority repair still lets the exact key of the opposing unanchored seat act as an anchored seat after that key resolves to the anchored seat's persistent identity. matchSeat checks identity collision only when the other seat has already upgraded; it does not reject record.Actor == other.actor. A sequence can anchor both keys to A, let white upgrade, withdraw black's anchor so black makes a legal black move as its exact key, re-anchor black to A, then use the black key for white on the next turn. This violates the one-identity/one-seat boundary and requires a deterministic regression before item 4 can be reported."}